    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p>The region is bounded by the circle centered at the origin with radius <m>2</m>. This circle has equation <m>x^2 + y^2 = 4</m>. Thus the region of integration is</p>
<p><m>\begin{array}{lcl} R\amp =\amp  \left \lbrace (x,y) \, |\, -2 \le x \le 2, 
-\sqrt{4-x^2 } \le y \le \sqrt{4-x^2} \right \rbrace \\
\amp =\amp  \left \lbrace (x,y) \, |\, -2 \le y \le 2,
-\sqrt{4-y^2 } \le x \le \sqrt{4-y^2} \right \rbrace \end{array}</m></p>
<p>(a) <m>\displaystyle \iint_R f(x,y) dA = \int_{-2}^{2} \int_{\sqrt{4-x^2}}^{\sqrt{4-x^2}} f(x,y) \, dy \, dx</m></p>
<p>(b) <m>\displaystyle  \iint_R f(x,y) dA = \int_{-2}^{2} \int_{\sqrt{4-y^2}}^{\sqrt{4-y^2}} f(x,y) \, dx \, dy</m></p>
</solution>
